KONOHAGAKURE — ANBU SELECTION PROCESS
CLASSIFICATION: Restricted.

The ANBU (Ansatsu Sentou Tokushu Butai) are the Hokage's masked special-operations corps, handling assassination, high-risk reconnaissance, and guard duties, answering directly to the Hokage.

Process:
- Candidates are drawn from proven jonin and exceptional chunin displaying elite skill, discretion, and emotional control.
- Selection and induction are conducted in secret; membership is not publicly acknowledged.
- Inductees receive an animal-motif mask and a codename; their true identity is sealed for the duration of service.
- Operatives are expected to subordinate personal identity to the mission.

The Root sub-division operated under separate, more severe conditioning and is documented under S-rank restriction. ANBU service is a matter of village record kept from general access.
Issued under direct Hokage authority.
